<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy and Personal Data Notice" lang="en">
  <article class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy and Personal Data Notice</h1>

    <h2>Privacy — Personal Data Management</h2>
    <p>Francesco Montelli processes your data in compliance with European Regulation (EU) 2016/679 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data.</p>
    <p>Under current European cookie regulations, all websites are required to inform users about the use of cookies on the site.</p>

    <h2>Data Controller</h2>
    <p>The data controller for all data collected on this site is <strong>Francesco Montelli</strong>.</p>

    <h2>Types of Data Processed</h2>

    <h3>Navigation Data</h3>
    <p>The computer systems and software procedures used to operate this site collect, in the course of their normal operation, certain data whose transmission is implicit in the use of Internet communication protocols. Francesco Montelli never collects such data in a form that allows users to be identified.</p>
    <p>This category of data includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP addresses or domain names of the computers used by users connecting to the site</li>
      <li>URI (Uniform Resource Identifier) addresses of the requested resources</li>
      <li>The time of the request</li>
      <li>The method used to submit the request to the server</li>
      <li>The size of the file received in response</li>
      <li>The numeric code indicating the status of the server's response (success, error, etc.)</li>
      <li>Other parameters relating to the user's operating system and computing environment</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This data is used exclusively in anonymous form and for statistical purposes related to site usage and proper functioning.</p>

    <h3>Data Voluntarily Provided by the User</h3>
    <p>Personal data may be collected voluntarily through:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sending email to the addresses listed on the site</li>
      <li>Submitting electronic forms on the site</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Sending an email involves the collection of the sender's email address, which is necessary to respond to the request, as well as any other personal data contained in the message. Personal data collected in this way will be used solely to reply to the received email and for any subsequent related communications.</p>
    <p>Submitting information request forms involves the collection of information sent through those forms.</p>

    <h2>General Information on Cookies</h2>
    <p>When you access a website, it or related sites may set or read cookies and/or other types of identifiers on the browser and/or device you are using.</p>
    <p>A cookie is a small text file stored on the computer of a website visitor in order to record certain information about the visit and to create a way to recognise the user at later times. Device identifiers, on the other hand, are generated by collecting and processing information such as IP address and/or user agent (browser version, type and version of operating system) or other device characteristics, also to associate certain information with a specific user.</p>
    <p>A website can only set a cookie in a browser if the browser's configured preferences allow it. It is important to know that a browser will only allow a given website to access cookies set by that same site, not those set by other websites — there is no privacy risk in this regard.</p>

    <h2>Use of Cookies</h2>
    <p>This site uses cookies to make its services simple and efficient for users browsing its pages.</p>

    <h3>Types of Cookies Used</h3>
    <p>Below are the types of cookies used by this site according to their purpose:</p>

    <h4>Technical Cookies</h4>
    <p>This type of cookie enables the correct functioning of certain sections of the site. They fall into two categories:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Persistent</strong>: not destroyed when the browser is closed; they remain until a preset expiry date</li>
      <li><strong>Session</strong>: destroyed every time the browser is closed</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These cookies, always sent from our domain, are necessary for the site to display correctly and in relation to the technical services offered. They will therefore always be used and sent, unless the user modifies their browser settings (which may affect how site pages are displayed).</p>

    <h4>Analytical Cookies</h4>
    <p>Cookies in this category are used to collect information about site usage in the form of anonymous statistical analysis. This type of cookie collects data anonymously about user activity and how users arrived at the site. Analytical cookies are sent by the site itself.</p>

    <h4>Traffic Analysis (cookie-free)</h4>
    <p>This site uses <strong>Umami</strong> (<a href="https://umami.is" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">umami.is</a>) as a traffic analytics tool. Umami does not use cookies, does not collect personally identifiable data, and does not perform cross-site tracking. The data collected (pages visited, referrer, device type, browser, country of origin) is aggregated and anonymised: it does not allow individual visitors to be identified in any way.</p>

    <h2>Cookie Consent</h2>
    <p>Under current regulations, this site is not required to request consent for technical and analytical cookies.</p>
    <p>For all other types of cookies, consent may be given by the user in one or more of the following ways:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Through specific configurations of the browser being used or related software programs used to browse the pages of the site</li>
      <li>By modifying settings when using third-party services</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Either of these solutions may prevent the user from using or viewing parts of the site.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
